From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 05:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinephone-pro: reserve memory for ramoops

The phone has no reachable serial console and CONFIG_PSTORE was off, so a
kernel oops or a hang leaves nothing behind at all: the journal cannot be
flushed once the machine stops, and the next boot starts with a clean slate.

Measured on 2026-09-19: the phone entered suspend at 21:39:01, the kernel
printed its "Filesystems sync" line, and nothing followed. It stayed that way
for eight hours - USB still enumerated, no response on any interface - and the
only way out was a forced power-off. With no crash log there is no way to see
which device or task stalled on the way into suspend.

Reserve a megabyte for ramoops so the console ring survives a reset. Unlike
the PineTab2 (rk3566), which can use the Rockchip BSP window at 0x110000,
RK3399 gives the kernel no RAM below 0x00200000 - the first two megabytes
belong to ATF - so a fixed low address is not available here. Let the kernel
place the region instead: reserved-memory allocates it early and
deterministically for a given kernel and memory map, which is all pstore needs
to find its records again after a warm reset.

console-size dominates the split on purpose: a hang produces no oops record,
and the console ring is then the only evidence of what the kernel was doing.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts
@@ -31,6 +31,35 @@
 		stdout-path = "serial2:115200n8";
 	};
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		/*
+		 * Keep a crash log across a reset. RK3399 gives the kernel no
+		 * RAM below 0x00200000 - the first two megabytes belong to ATF
+		 * - so the PineTab2's BSP window at 0x110000 is not available
+		 * here. This address is where the kernel itself placed the
+		 * region when asked to allocate one, well clear of the image
+		 * u-boot loads at 0x02080000; a fixed reg is required because
+		 * the ramoops driver looks the resource up in the device tree
+		 * and refuses a dynamically allocated node ("failed to locate
+		 * DT /reserved-memory resource", -EINVAL).
+		 *
+		 * console-size dominates on purpose: a hang produces no oops
+		 * record and the console ring is then the only evidence.
+		 */
+		ramoops@1ff00000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x1ff00000 0x0 0x00100000>;
+			console-size = <0x80000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x20000>;
+			ftrace-size = <0x00000>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	adc-keys {
 		compatible = "adc-keys";
 		io-channels = <&saradc 1>;
